Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Regional settings: English (Canada), the standards and formats of Windows' en-CA, the location Canada and 24-hour time.
;
; ReactOS reads all of this from HKCU\Control Panel\International (kernel32 and the Regional Options applet, intl.cpl); the logon box
; and the system use HKU\.DEFAULT, so both get the same values. The user locale is `Locale`, a hex string that winlogon passes to
; NtSetDefaultLocale at logon. The time format is `sTimeFormat`: the taskbar clock calls GetTimeFormat with no format and
; TIME_NOSECONDS, so "HH:mm:ss" shows 14:55 there and 14:55:07 in the Regional Options sample. `iTime`, `iTLZero` and `iTimePrefix` are
; what the applet's Time dialog shows (24-hour clock, leading zero, no prefix). The system locale is Nls\Language "Default"; the keyboard
; layout and `InstallLanguage` (the language of the user interface) stay as they are.
;
; The Default User profile template (the NTUSER.DAT a new account copies) is not changed.
;
